WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Nina, Mom is at Miša's.

2
00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:35.790
That's right, I don't live with Mom anymore. She's my past.

3
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.840
Kitty, kitty, kitty, kitty. Kiki, where are you? Kitty?

4
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.790
So where's Kiki? Kiki is dead. Mom, Dad ran her over with the car.

5
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.790
God, son, what are you saying? Your dad is dead!

6
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.790
Don't tell me that. If we hadn't buried him together, I wouldn't have known.

7
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.790
First he ran over the cat, and then he died.

8
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.790
So we definitely don't have a cat?

9
00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.790
No puppy, no kitten, no dad.

10
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.880
But there was some cat here.

11
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:04.180
You mixed it up, Rosa, we were looking after the neighbor's cat. She's not called Kiki, she's Ljubica.

12
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.230
And I took her back last night.

13
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.300
God, then why did I buy all this?

14
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.240
Come on, come on, at least you have breakfast.

15
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.200
Have you ever heard me meow?

16
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:20.320
Oh come on, I boiled you an egg. I'll bring it right now, hard-boiled, just the way you like it.

17
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.920
Rosa, bring that egg and sit here, we need to agree on something.

18
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.880
Hey, shall we buy a cat? I'd love one.

19
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:31.710
No.

20
00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.420
Well all right, then we could get a canary, a nice little one.

21
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.680
Rosa, please, just sit down here once so we can talk.

22
00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.580
Fine, all right. What should we talk about?

23
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.580
About your move. What move?

24
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.720
We agreed you'd go to Miša and Jovanka's, you remember perfectly well.

25
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.540
God, Milentije, what are you saying? You've been stringing me along here for a week.

26
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.220
You should have left last Thursday.

27
00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:05.820
You know what? There's a great pet shop across the street.

28
00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.780
They sell canaries, as many as you like. If you only knew how nicely they chirp.

29
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.140
Rosa, it's no use changing the subject. Your things are packed. Miša is coming to take you.

30
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.870
Where is he taking me? I don't understand you at all.

31
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.450
You never understand anything. Whenever I want to talk to you seriously,

32
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.140
Rosa suddenly turns senile. Rosa suddenly forgets everything.

33
00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.580
Come on, eat that egg. It's hard-boiled. Sit down!

34
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.180
I can't sit. My tailbone hurts.

35
00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.460
But Rosa, people have to sit for breakfast, lunch and dinner.

36
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.230
God, since when have you become so traditional?

37
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.100
Since you talked my wife into leaving me?

38
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.520
Son, she wasn't right for you anyway.

39
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.280
Well, now she'll come back, and you'll nicely go there and look after Miša's kids.

40
00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.900
Come on, eat that egg. It's hard-boiled. Boiled, I know.

41
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:11.630
Only you could lose the car key inside the car!

42
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.680
Where else would I lose it? Wait!

43
00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.630
Here you go! Man, the way you and I solve everything!

44
00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.630
The two of us solve the toughest situation.

45
00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:32.830
Yes, except there was never just the two of us, there were always three! No more Rosa. Now we're alone.

46
00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.130
Then why didn't we meet at your apartment instead of in this vehicle?

47
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:40.330
At my apartment? Where would I get an apartment, man?

48
00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.130
Because I want to do something in it, so that when you walk in, it's something different.

49
00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:49.970
You want to repaint? Well, come on, don't spoil the surprise.

50
00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.020
And when can I come over?

51
00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:10.220
Come on, my love, get out, please. I'll call you, seriously, I'll call you on the landline. You'll call, you'll call.

52
00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:38.750
Rosa! Rosa, Mom! Mom!

53
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.500
Slava's sweater, the one with diamonds, I don't know whether it needs ironing or not.

54
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.020
Rosa, take off the headphones!

55
00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:07.370
Oh, son, I just can't remember whether the Beatles had Yesterday on the album Help or Revolver.

56
00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.530
Ask Miša, he's coming now. I didn't even know he was coming.

57
00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:20.590
Thank God, here he is. Coming, brother, just a moment! Come in, brother!

58
00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.390
What's going on here? Why can't I get into this house?

59
00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.200
What have you done to the house? Why is there a bicycle here? She rides a bicycle.

60
00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:36.200
She rides a bicycle? That'll harm her. Are you normal? Is she all right?

61
00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:40.200
Your house is falling apart. Nothing works, not even the doorbell.

62
00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.200
You sent me some Chinese guy, he unscrewed the doorbell and left.

63
00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.200
I got you the contact. Keep working with him, agree something, let him give the doorbell back.

64
00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:50.200
Is Mom all right? Is Mom all right? Where's Mom?

65
00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:57.200
Mommy, where's my mommy? Mom, oh Mom, my mom.

66
00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:02.190
Mom, look what I brought you, Mommy, cream cakes, just for you.

67
00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:10.070
Are you normal? Do you know how high her sugar jumps? No, I'm a doctor, I know, a little sugar never killed anyone.

68
00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.390
Then why did you bring so many?

69
00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:20.430
Listen, go over there, put it in the fridge, and I'll tell you how and on which days to eat it.

70
00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:25.590
Why are you doing this? She's your mother, that woman gave birth to you.

71
00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.210
What's going on with you? Why are you so negative?

72
00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.890
Hey, what's happening with your house?

73
00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:35.190
Look, where do I go in? Can I sit here?

74
00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:43.750
Why is the house so neglected? Do you want me to bring you workmen to fix this? I know the best workmen in town.

75
00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.670
Don't bring me anybody, just take my mother away.

76
00:06:55.590 --> 00:07:03.390
An extremely strange person. I did that nose brilliantly. I told her, be careful, when you blow it, don't shake it.

77
00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.250
She blew it and shook it, and blew it and shook it.

78
00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:14.090
She shook it so much that the nose finally fell off. Sorry, I can't give a warranty on craziness. Please excuse me, I have a missed call.

79
00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:26.030
Hello? Hi, my love? Dragana? Who is Dragana? I don't know, I don't know who Dragana is. What does she want? I'm telling you, I don't know who Dragana is.

80
00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.620
I mean, I don't know which Dragana that is.

81
00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:35.380
What? That's disinformation, my love, you're important to me. You're the most important to me.

82
00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:44.740
Oh no. You're sinning against your conscience, Joka, you're sinning. Do I look like a man who would pass himself off as a bachelor?

83
00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:50.420
Oh, my Joka. You're sinning against your conscience, Joka, you really are.

84
00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:55.040
I booked for the two of us, my love. Hey, you know what a wonderful place it is?

85
00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.980
Okay, when I get back, we'll sort it all out.

86
00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:04.420
Okay, I love you and I kiss you. Bye, bye, bye, bye.

87
00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.640
Why? So you won't take her?

88
00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.470
I can't tonight, please. I can't, please.

89
00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:15.920
You know what Joka is like. Joka will kill me if I bring Mom tonight.

90
00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.010
Well, at least tomorrow then.

91
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.480
Right, I have breasts, breasts, eyelids, eyelids, eyelids.

92
00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:27.840
Can you? Tomorrow I can't. Can you? I can in seventeen days.

93
00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:32.890
Then find one free day to come to my funeral, because I'm going to kill myself?

94
00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:38.750
If it's no trouble, see that it's next month, since I have two noses to do, but also a pile of eyelids.

95
00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.760
You've all let me down. Fine, nothing for it, I'll just hang myself from the chandelier.

96
00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:50.340
Mile, what's wrong with you? What are these dark thoughts? Get out of that tunnel.

97
00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:56.460
Do you want me to help? Do you want me to fix up this house? Do you want me to give you money? How much money do you need?

98
00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.080
Fifty euros? A hundred euros? Two hundred euros? Do you want money?

99
00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:11.990
But who guarantees me that you'll be able to put up with that woman? She's your mother. That woman gave birth to you, that woman gave you life.

100
00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:18.100
Well, that woman who gave me life drove away my ex-wife, who now wants to come back to me.

101
00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:24.180
Listen to me, I convinced Nina to come back, but I told her I no longer live with Mom.

102
00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:30.220
That's why it's desperately necessary for Mom to go to your place. Then I agreed with you that you'd take her today,

103
00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:38.810
but you don't want to take her, because suddenly, by some miracle, Joka wants to kill you, and Mom of course suddenly doesn't remember any agreement.

104
00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:49.860
Milentije, I have only two words for you. You don't lie to a woman. And two more words. Nursing home.

105
00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:57.810
Let go of my hand, you primitive. In the civilized world that's what people do, you normal man.

106
00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:02.810
We'll leave her there, we'll pay for the home. We'll split the cost in half.

107
00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:13.580
Fine, paying, I'm not making a problem. When money isn't an issue, they bathe her there, feed her, take care of her, service her, maintain her.

108
00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.340
We drop by now and then, play with her a bit, and everyone's calm.

109
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.200
Fine, but we tell her this together. Is that a deal? Is it clear?

110
00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:26.110
Brother, brother, of course it's a deal. My dear brother, a good deal.

111
00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:36.500
Kids, let me ask you something. Do these Beatles have their Yesterday? Is it on the album Help or Revolver?

112
00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.140
How many cream cakes did you eat?

113
00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:43.960
God, God, baby, why do you worry about what I eat and how much I eat?

114
00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:15.410
You ate eight cream cakes, Rosa. What do you mean, ate? Eight! How many? Are you deaf, eight!

115
00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:23.360
You're too literal, you know. Do you know how high her sugar is now, like Mount Everest. A living person can't survive that.

116
00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:27.410
My God, you don't know what I've been through.

117
00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:35.360
Mile, let's do it this way: you know Mom loves sweets. I'm a doctor, I know, it won't hurt her.

118
00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:41.130
If I thought cream cakes were unhealthy, I wouldn't bring them to her. You should at least know how much I care about Mom.

119
00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.430
Mom is the most important to me. Sorry, I have to answer.

120
00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:49.570
Hello, darling, I'm here. Darling, you're the most important to me, what are you talking about?

121
00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:54.310
Well, all right, all right, bye, bye, bye. I apologize, I have to go.

122
00:11:54.650 --> 00:12:04.350
Let's agree like this. Call me, don't hesitate. If there's a problem, you just dial. I'm here for everything, anything you need, Mom.

123
00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.810
You can rely on me freely.

124
00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:20.760
I'll send you the best workmen to fix this. Mom, I kiss you, brother, I kiss you, I'm off. Bye, bye!

125
00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:28.760
You see how wonderful Miša is, how attentive. I'm the most important to him, even though he has a wife and kids.

126
00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:33.760
That Miša, to whom you're the most important, has just suggested that we put you in a home.

127
00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:39.790
Oh, shame on you! He suggested that to me, Mom.

128
00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:50.630
Don't lie, you hear? Well, there, you've bitten me right in the heart. It wasn't me who said that, Mom, Miša said it.

129
00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:55.590
Mom, please, don't be angry, Mom! Mom, please!

130
00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:12.420
Have you seen everything? What do you think of the whole building? This is our library, you see?

131
00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.280
Great, really nice. Nice. Please, have a seat. Thank you.

132
00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:21.370
Tell me something about your mother.

133
00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:25.770
Well, she's a very lively woman. She had a strange childhood.

134
00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:29.750
My grandfather was Tito's general, so she grew up in a very strange atmosphere.

135
00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:37.310
He wanted to instill military discipline in her, so the poor girl woke up at six every morning until she was 12, to the sound of a bugle.

136
00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.290
He blew the bugle, yes. And then she had to march around the house.

137
00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:45.380
And my father was also military, but neither of them managed to make her conform.

138
00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:49.380
While her friends listen to classical music, she's still going wild to rock and roll.

139
00:13:49.430 --> 00:14:00.880
So what else can I say, she has another son, my brother. He's a plastic surgeon, but she loves him more than me. Probably because I'm the one who looks after her.

140
00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:06.880
You're under stress now because of your mother. But she'll have more than a great time here.

141
00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:16.830
You know how it is, in every hotel there's some guest who's a little strange.

142
00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:32.320
Your mother will have tenderness, attention, love and care here. And food? That too. Oh, good.

143
00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:41.280
You know how to put it, she'll now be staying away from her apartment for a bit longer for the first time.

144
00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:46.140
In the apartment where we live now, she's lived her whole life. She was born there. And I was born there too.

145
00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:52.800
She didn't want to go to the maternity ward, she gave birth to me on the marital bed because she wanted to watch the last episode of "Otpisani". She didn't want to miss it.

146
00:14:53.560 --> 00:15:00.260
What I mean is, you see, I'd like to place her here with you, but not at any price.

147
00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:09.280
Well, these are our prices. You'll see, it's only a small contribution toward the love and attention we give our eldest.

148
00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:13.440
Oh God, Lord. Tell me how much it would cost without love, just care and food?

149
00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:19.550
I understand it's hard for you. Nobody loves a mother more than a son.

150
00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:27.710
I suggest, if you can't decide, that you give me your brother's phone number so I can talk to him too.

151
00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:35.610
When will I be able to visit her? Whenever you like. Thursdays from 12 to 2. Except the first Thursday of the month.

152
00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:42.050
That's when we do rodent and insect control. We must look after the hygiene of our dear ones.

153
00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:48.290
Yes, yes, right, right, right. I only ask one thing at the end: be gentle with her.

154
00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:54.100
This is the first time she's coming to a nursing home. And your turn will come too, and I'll be waiting for you.

155
00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:07.340
Whose suitcase is this? Which suitcase?

156
00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:20.250
Mom, we said only the bare essentials. You'll be there three, four days. And if you don't like it, no harm done.

157
00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:27.050
Oh no, I like my suitcase. If I didn't like it, I wouldn't have bought it, you know?

158
00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.610
I didn't mean the suitcase, I meant the home.

159
00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:40.770
Mom, you'll be in a nice hotel and you'll socialize with people your age.

160
00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:52.100
But listen, I really think I shouldn't leave you alone. Because you see how forgetful you've become. Look, you didn't even buy me a canary.

161
00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:57.150
Come on, let's go to the market. I'll buy you the most beautiful canary there is.

162
00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:13.650
Son, Dad told me that rooms like this are where they kept prisoners after the war. Take me out of here.

163
00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:26.900
Easy now, Mom. Look, see, the bed is comfortable. You'll be fine here. You have a nice view.

164
00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:34.160
And I brought you a canary to keep you entertained. To entertain me, to sing me a swan song.

165
00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:42.730
Ah, you've settled in. I don't think I asked you anything. And I don't know why you're addressing me at all.

166
00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:45.380
Mom, nobody attacked you, take it easy.

167
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:52.260
You told me there'd be some luxury here, this is Goli Otok. Love, tenderness, attention.

168
00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:55.560
And now, please, wait for me outside and we'll talk.

169
00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:02.900
There, come on, Radmila, tell us how you like it here.

170
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:09.560
Stay here, sun of a foreign sky, it won't warm you the way this one does.

171
00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:16.280
There, we've been reading Aleksa Šantić. And you, Rosa, could learn "The Blue Tomb".

172
00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.340
We care about educating our patients.

173
00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:27.660
There, devote yourself to "The Blue Tomb".

174
00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:32.440
Let me tell you something. I don't eat eggs for dinner.

175
00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:41.670
I only eat white turkey meat, boiled vegetables, unleavened rye bread, and a glass of red wine.

176
00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:47.120
See you later. Dinner. God.

177
00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:58.540
It's all balanced. Nutri, tooti, fruti, eat and keep quiet.

178
00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:54.390
Nina! Nina, good evening. Nina! Nina, good evening.

179
00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.440
So where are you, Nina?

180
00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:07.100
You smell so nice, you know?

181
00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:09.880
You look good.

182
00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:31.570
And your apartment is somehow masculine?

183
00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:38.660
Shall we eat now?

184
00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:42.660
Oh, I forgot the food. What's wrong with you, man?

185
00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:44.660
You know that whenever I eat my fill, I fall asleep.

186
00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:48.660
And do you still snore? Only on Mondays.

187
00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:52.710
And what exactly were you thinking about when you forgot the food? About Mom.

188
00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:59.660
God, you've somehow changed. You've somehow become more serious.

189
00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:11.100
Does this serious Milentije now have some serious desires too? He does. Which ones? Leave your right hand free so you can cross yourself.

190
00:22:11.150 --> 00:22:16.150
This is the moment when your mother won't barge in on us. Never again.

191
00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:27.530
Is someone ringing? No, no. Is someone ringing? No, no. It's a wrong number.

192
00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:34.030
Someone's ringing the door, man. No, believe me. It's not the phone. The door!

193
00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:44.210
Oh, fine, come on, just open it already, man.

194
00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:56.420
Good evening. Good evening.

195
00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:18.390
I'll be very direct. We did take your mother into the home. However, we'd like to return her to you.

196
00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:24.230
That's out of the question, I paid. No, no, please, I brought the money to give back to you.

197
00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:29.690
Who is this? Go back in there, I'll be right there, I'll sort this out, and we'll continue where we left off.

198
00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:34.130
Here, the staff also collected some money, please.

199
00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:39.630
Excuse me, and what about Rosa? She was causing disorder in the nursing home.

200
